      "body": "## Problem\n\n`test_causal_conv1d_nwh_autograd[fp64-k4-silu]` and `[fp64-k4-identity]` fail on devices with about 99 KB of shared memory per block. cuDNN 9.27 declines the FP64 NWH forward there with status 3010 (`CUDNN_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED_SHARED_MEMORY_INSUFFICIENT`), which the binding raises as `RuntimeError: cudnnCausalConv1dNwhForward failed with status 3010`. The other dtypes in the same test run normally.\n\n| device | develop 97b7bc31 |\n|---|---|\n| RTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0) | 2 failed, 37 passed |\n| L40S (cc 8.9) | 2 failed, 37 passed |\n\n## Change\n\n`test_causal_conv1d_nwh_autograd` skips when the NWH call fails with status 3010 and quotes the backend's message in the skip reason. Any other error still fails the test. Nothing outside this test changes.\n\n## Tests\n\nOn an RTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0) with cuDNN 9.27, `test/python/causal_conv1d/torch/test_causal_conv1d.py` gives 37 passed, 2 skipped with this change (develop: 2 failed, 37 passed). The skip reason reads `cuDNN reports insufficient shared memory for this NWH case on this device: cudnnCausalConv1dNwhForward failed with status 3010`. `pre-commit` passes.\n",
