      "body": "**Codex bot review · model: `gpt-6-astra`**\n\nReviewed `6770fff18f3d` against base `97b7bc3128d6`.\n\nThank you for your contribution! The skip is limited to the reported forward shared-memory rejection, and supported FP64 cases still run their numerical checks. I found no defect. Approval is deferred for workflow and CI gates.\n\nValidation: Ten controlled error-injection checks passed against the exact head and baseline test functions. Only the head's forward RuntimeError with status 3010 becomes a skip. Other forward statuses, a non-RuntimeError and a backward status-3010 failure propagate unchanged; the baseline still raises for forward status 3010. Both FP64 NWH cases passed on native SM100 with cuDNN 9.26, including output and input/weight/bias gradient comparisons. The exact Python source and unchanged compatible extension were verified. Reviewed the full test and its reference. Status 3010 denotes insufficient shared memory; backward and numerical assertions remain outside the catch. Tolerances, production code and kernels are unchanged. Precheck found no candidates.\n\nLimitations: The broader native sweep reached its 120-second limit before completion; no full-suite pass is claimed. No local low-shared-memory-device run was made, so the author's SM120 result remains separate evidence. Style and Security require maintainer approval. The applicable python/misc CI route remains held after its known pre-test authentication failure; no retry or alternate route was used.\n\nReview incomplete; approval is deferred.\n\n<!-- codex-fe-review:v2:2215:6770fff18f3d2e27e4856b406200d9ae15ccfec5:deferred:no-blocker -->",
